From: Fredrik Foss-Indrehus <fredrik@ffoss.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026
Subject: Realign the stack in the crash handler's entry point on x86

GTKNoCSDMain is the ELF entry point when the library is started as the
crash handler. The kernel enters it with a 16-byte aligned stack and no
return address, so the function runs 8 bytes off the alignment the
System V AMD64 ABI promises; the first SSE instruction on a stack
buffer faults. On target the handler died with a general protection
fault in GTKNoCSDSaveArguments (pcmpeqb on the 8 KiB cmdline buffer)
once crash-handler-initialise-arguments.patch made it get that far.

Origin: backport, https://codeberg.org/MorsMortium/GTK-NoCSD/commit/664d8c6
Applied-Upstream: 4.0
Last-Update: 2026-09-24
---
--- a/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
+++ b/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
@@ -138,7 +138,13 @@
 	}
 }
 
+// Requires stack realignment because bypassing the C runtime startup leaves
+// the stack unaligned, violating the System V AMD64 ABI.
+#if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
+__attribute__((visibility("default"), force_align_arg_pointer))
+#else
 __attribute__((visibility("default")))
+#endif
 void GTKNoCSDMain(void) {
 	// This runs when the library is started as an executable
 
